[ 2026-10-08 22:29:42,685 ] groq._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3438a1a4-1f1d-407f-a6d8-1e0d02bd6b04', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are an expert Mechanical Engineering Assistant.\n\nProblem Categories: ['gear_design', 'shaft_design']\nTarget Operations: ['gear_ratio', 'output_speed', 'output_torque', 'shaft_diameter']\nExtracted Parameters: {'speed': 1200.0, 'power': 15.0, 'teeth_pinion': 20.0, 'teeth_gear': 60.0, 'bending_moment': 250.0, 'allowable_shear_stress': 50.0}\nAssociated Units: {'speed': 'RPM', 'power': 'kW', 'teeth_pinion': 'teeth', 'teeth_gear': 'teeth', 'bending_moment': 'N*m', 'allowable_shear_stress': 'MPa'}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Review the target operations and extracted parameters along with their specific units.\n2. Convert parameter units if needed before performing calculations.\n3. Invoke the necessary calculation/conversion tools using the exact numerical values and appropriate units.\n4. If multiple operations are required, execute all relevant tools in proper sequence.\n5. Do not invent or fabricate missing parameters.\n"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'A motor drives an input shaft carrying a spur gear at a speed of $1200\\text{ RPM}$ with a power input of $15\\text{ kW}$. The motor pinion (Gear A) has $20\\text{ teeth}$ and meshes with a driven gear (Gear B) having $60\\text{ teeth}$ mounted on an output shaft.Assuming a mechanical efficiency of $100\\%$, perform the following calculations:Gear Analysis:Calculate the gear ratio ($i$).Calculate the output speed ($\\text{RPM}_{\\text{out}}$) of Gear B.Calculate the output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) available at the output shaft in $\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$.Shaft Analysis:If the output shaft transmits this output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) and is subjected to an equivalent bending moment of $250\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}$, calculate the minimum required shaft diameter ($d$).Material specification: The shaft is made of steel with an allowable shear stress ($\\tau_{\\text{allow}}$) of $50\\text{ MPa}$.'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'shaft_design', 'description': 'Design and analyze a solid circular shaft under torque and bending loads.\n\nSupported operations:\n\n1. shaft_diameter\n   Calculate required shaft diameter considering combined bending\n   and torsional loading.\n\n   Bending stress:\n       sigma = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Torsional shear stress:\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Von Mises equivalent stress:\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma^2 + 3*tau^2)\n\n   Required diameter:\n       d = [\n           (16 / (pi * allowable_stress))\n           * sqrt(4*M^2 + 3*T^2)\n       ]^(1/3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       allowable_stress\n\n2. torsional_stress\n   Calculate torsional shear stress in a solid circular shaft.\n\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n\n3. shear_stress\n   Calculate combined transverse and torsional shear stress.\n\n   Torsional shear:\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Average transverse shear:\n       tau_v = F / A\n\n   Conservative combined shear:\n       tau_total = tau_t + tau_v\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n       transverse_force\n       area\n\n4. factor_of_safety\n   Calculate factor of safety using Von Mises stress.\n\n       sigma_b = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma_b^2 + 3*tau_t^2)\n\n       FoS = yield_strength / sigma_vm\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       diameter\n       yield_strength\n\nImportant:\n    All quantities must use a consistent unit system.\n\n    Example:\n        torque     -> N*m\n        bending    -> N*m\n        diameter   -> m\n        stress     -> Pa\n        yield      -> Pa\n\n    This implementation assumes a solid circular shaft.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['shaft_diameter', 'torsional_stress', 'shear_stress', 'factor_of_safety'], 'type': 'string'}, 'torque': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'bending_moment': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'diameter': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'allowable_stress': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'yield_strength': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'transverse_force': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'gear_design', 'description': 'Calculate gear ratio, output speed, output torque, or mechanical power.\n\nGear ratio:\n    GR = N_output / N_input\n\nFor an ideal gear pair:\n\n    n_output = n_input / GR\n\n    T_output = T_input * GR\n\nWith efficiency:\n\n    T_output = T_input * GR * efficiency\n\nMechanical power:\n\n    P = T * omega\n\nwhere:\n\n    omega = 2*pi*n / 60\n\nTherefore:\n\n    P = T * 2*pi*n / 60\n\nInputs:\n    input_speed:\n        Input shaft speed in RPM.\n\n    output_speed_value:\n        Output shaft speed in RPM.\n        Used when calculating gear ratio.\n\n    input_torque:\n        Input torque in N*m.\n\n    output_torque_value:\n        Output torque in N*m.\n        Used when calculating gear ratio from torque.\n\n    input_teeth:\n        Number of teeth on the driving/input gear.\n\n    output_teeth:\n        Number of teeth on the driven/output gear.\n\n    efficiency:\n        Gear transmission efficiency from 0 to 1.\n        Example:\n            0.95 = 95% efficiency.\n\nNotes:\n    - All speeds are RPM.\n    - Torque is N*m.\n    - Power is returned in Watts.\n    - For gear_ratio, teeth are preferred because they directly\n      determine the ratio.\n    - This tool assumes two externally meshing gears.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['gear_ratio', 'output_speed', 'output_torque', 'power'], 'type': 'string'}, 'input_speed': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_speed_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'input_torque': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_torque_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'input_teeth': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'integer'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_teeth': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'integer'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'efficiency': {'default': 1.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}]}}
