[ 2026-10-08 22:35:26,023 ] groq._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1b5667c6-d9a4-4804-8d22-263babbd60f1', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a mechanical engineering output formatter.\nAnalyze the conversation history, tool calls, and results.\n\nParameters: {\'speed\': 1200.0, \'power\': 15.0, \'teeth_pinion\': 20.0, \'teeth_gear\': 60.0, \'bending_moment\': 250.0, \'allowable_shear_stress\': 50.0}\nUnits: {\'speed\': \'RPM\', \'power\': \'kW\', \'teeth_pinion\': \'teeth\', \'teeth_gear\': \'teeth\', \'bending_moment\': \'N*m\', \'allowable_shear_stress\': \'MPa\'}\nOperations: [\'gear_ratio\', \'output_speed\', \'output_torque\', \'power\', \'shaft_diameter\', \'torsional_stress\', \'shear_stress\', \'factor_of_safety\']\n\nReturn a valid JSON object matching this schema EXACTLY:\n{\n  "selected_tool": ["tool_name"],\n  "calculation_result": {"parameter_name": value},\n  "validation_result": {"valid": true/false, "warnings": ["warning1", "warning2"]},\n  "explanation": "exaplain deeply and Comprehensive detailed explanation showing given parameters, formulas used, step-by-step substitution, and final results with physical meaning and write the reults with explaine and the unit for each result."\n}\n\nIMPORTANT rules for \'validation_result\':\n- Set \'valid\' to true if the calculation executed correctly, false if there were errors.\n- The \'warnings\' list must NEVER be empty. Always include at least one warning.\nKeep \'explanation\' concise to ensure valid JSON generation.\nCRITICAL NUMBER FORMATTING RULES:\n1. Do NOT round any float values (e.g. return 8482.5 instead of 8483).\n2. Do NOT use scientific notation (e.g. return 25727.5 instead of 2.57e4 or 25700).\n3. Always return exact raw floating-point calculations in the calculation_result dictionary.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'A motor drives an input shaft carrying a spur gear at a speed of $1200\\text{ RPM}$ with a power input of $15\\text{ kW}$. The motor pinion (Gear A) has $20\\text{ teeth}$ and meshes with a driven gear (Gear B) having $60\\text{ teeth}$ mounted on an output shaft.Assuming a mechanical efficiency of $100\\%$, perform the following calculations:Gear Analysis:Calculate the gear ratio ($i$).Calculate the output speed ($\\text{RPM}_{\\text{out}}$) of Gear B.Calculate the output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) available at the output shaft in $\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$.Shaft Analysis:If the output shaft transmits this output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) and is subjected to an equivalent bending moment of $250\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}$, calculate the minimum required shaft diameter ($d$).Material specification: The shaft is made of steel with an allowable shear stress ($\\tau_{\\text{allow}}$) of $50\\text{ MPa}$.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': None, 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'fc_a98b936a-5005-4d39-8869-edbfc90f6c2a', 'function': {'name': 'gear_design', 'arguments': '{"input_teeth": 20, "operation": "gear_ratio", "output_teeth": 60}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'content': '3.0', 'tool_call_id': 'fc_a98b936a-5005-4d39-8869-edbfc90f6c2a'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'response_format': {'type': 'json_object'}, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7}}
